@@ -9325,3 +9325,4 @@ Did NOT modify research-roadmap.yaml or scripts/research_conductor.py. Did NOT p
 - 2026-06-18: PHASE D (CROSS-DOMAIN DETECTION CALIBRATION + POOL EXPANSION; complementary; cheap; verifier_is_oracle=false) -- scale the .405 cross-domain detection win (exp4386, GAP-4 ARC AUROC 0.963 on ONE non-FoVer domain) into a CALIBRATED multi-domain detector contract (arXiv:2102.10395). .405 reached only one non-FoVer domain (code/GSM pools 'unavailable until labeled verifier-score pools exist'); this builds them from EXISTING cached candidates and calibrates. Score the detector against FoVer + GAP-4 ARC + code (HumanEval, cached results/experiment_1999_code_verification_humaneval.json / exp2838 / exp2839 -- unit_test_pass_flags oracle, headroom 0.18) + GSM8K (cached adversarial_gsm8k_data_400.json / exp1998). Apply LEAVE-ONE-DOMAIN-OUT calibration (temperature / Platt scaling fit on the other domains) and report detection AUROC + risk-coverage (selective risk at coverage) + the SELECTION-headroom PER domain -- the headline is the DIVERGENCE (detect where you cannot select) + whether calibration TRANSFERS across domains. Emit detection_calibrated_multi_domain BARE bool := (detection AUROC CI95 lower bound > 0.5 on >=2 NON-FoVer domains AND leave-one-domain-out calibration keeps expected-calibration-error below the uncalibrated baseline on the held-out domain). verifier_is_oracle=false. A win = a deployable multi-domain detector contract (the verifier-domain-expansion step, north-star §0 step 2); a domain where detection ~= chance is LOGGED as a missing-verifier gap (the product backlog). This is cross-domain DETECTION (AUROC where selection headroom varies), NOT the RETIRED cross-domain SELECTION axis (exp4314). Cached candidates, CPU, zero quota. NO new live inference; NO TRM training. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: calibrated_multi_domain_contract_false; results/experiment_4397_cross_domain_detection_calibration.json
 - 2026-06-18: PHASE E1 (SOTA-ingestion; mandatory per SOTA-Ingestion Cycle Discipline) -- ingest the SOTA for the .406 bleeding-edge forks (verifiable-process-data first-error LOCALIZATION; cross-domain detection CALIBRATION; the localizer-compounds self-learning axis; ARC E3 lookahead-fidelity-gated deeper solves) and MAP the strongest 3-5 methods onto the .407 roadmap, conditioned on the .406 outcomes (did the synthetic-data localizer beat the 0.096 ensemble baseline + survive the skeptic-proof? did it COMPOUND? did calibration TRANSFER cross-domain? did ARC reach deeper/tail levels via the fidelity gate?). Use the RELIABLE channel ONLY (scripts/sweep_clusters.py / sweep_semscholar.py + low-concurrency WebSearch/WebFetch) -- /deep-research is BANNED in-loop. Every method MUST carry a real, VERIFIED arXiv ID/URL (no citation = fabrication). FLAG A2D2 (2606.13565) + SEPO (2502.01384) verifier-as-reward GENERATOR-training as OUT-OF-BAND/operator-owned. Update research-studying.md (mark ingested) and emit flagged_for_v407 (the single strongest method for the .407 planner). (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: sota_ingestion_v407_mapped; results/experiment_4398_sota_ingestion_v407.json
 - 2026-06-18: PHASE E2 (INFRA/HYGIENE) -- registry/gaps hygiene + GAP-4 regression guard. (1) Reconcile ops/verifier_registry.yaml + ops/verifier_gaps.md + ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml with the .406 outcomes (the localizer result exp4392/4393 -- move GAP-FOVER-BIPRM-LOCALIZATION to status: building/filled if the localizer graduated; the localizer-compounds result exp4396; the cross-domain calibration + any new chance-detection gaps exp4397; new ARC reproduced levels from exp4394-4395). (2) Run the GAP-4 regression guard (the ARC oracle-distinct verifier-beats-vote result must not silently regress). (3) Verify the capstone verifier_is_oracle stamping fix is STILL durable (the .402 exp4355 fix; confirm the .406 capstone path inherits it). NO production verifier edits (audit-only per Verifier Authenticity Discipline). (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: registry_gaps_arc_reconciled_to_v406_truth_gap4_guard_passed_True_capstone_stamp_fix_durable_True; results/experiment_4399_registry_gaps_hygiene_gap4_guard.json
+- 2026-06-18: PHASE E3 (HARDWARE CONTINUITY; KV260 opportunistic per north-star §3) -- KV260 SSH-reachability + loaded-bitstream continuity check. Per north-star §3, KV260 is THE sovereignty story (drive to terminal, then freeze); GateMate/PolarFire are opportunistic-only. SSH-reachability precondition ONLY (NEVER a host SD-card precondition per KV260 SSH-Not-SD-Card Discipline). If the board is reachable, record the loaded overlay (xmutil listapps) + a lightweight liveness check (the carnot_ising bitstream UIO device present); if it is the terminal board-latency transcript, capture it. If unreachable -> honest_verdict blocked_kv260_ssh_unreachable (a clean documented skip, NOT a fabrication). This keeps the board visible in the milestone retro without burning a deep task slot. NO host SD-card-device precondition (the retired mechanism). NO TRM training. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=success_kv260_continuity_terminal_reached; results/experiment_4400_hardware_continuity_kv260.json
